{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"[operator-attested] AC(a) SATISFIED — and my earlier claim that it was satisfied was WRONG.\n\nCORRECTION FIRST. An earlier comment here reported AC(a) met on the strength of an 11-passing live\nrun. That was an over-claim: I verified the tests PASSED but never checked them against the\ncriterion's \"every method\" quantifier. Five methods had ZERO live coverage — add_label,\nset_relationship, get_issuelinks_map, map_remote_links, link_payload_for_relation. The completion\nverifier caught this and was right to refuse the close.\n\nTHAT GAP FOUND A REAL PRODUCTION BUG. The live test written to cover add_label failed on its first\nexecution against a real Jira:\n    AttributeError: 'JIRA' object has no attribute 'add_field_value'\nadd_label called self._client.add_field_value(remote_id, \"labels\", label), but that attribute does\nnot exist on jira.JIRA — only on jira.resources.Issue, with a TWO-argument signature. So add_label\nraised on EVERY invocation: the DC transport could never label an issue. It shipped because the\nmethod had no test at any tier, and the unit fake exposed no such attribute to contradict the wrong\ncall shape. Fixed in Gerrit 1071 (via the Issue resource, preserving append semantics so a\nconcurrent edit is not clobbered), with unit coverage, mutation-verified twice.\n\nEVIDENCE (run https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/30592710985, head f7bc22000,\njob \"jira DC harness smoke\", ubuntu-latest, real Jira 8.17.1 DC built and torn down):\n\n    [jira-live-canary] collected=12 executed=12 skipped=0\n    12 passed in 8.95s\n\nRead the canary line, not the tick: executed=12 skipped=0 is what makes this evidence rather than a\ngreen no-op — the same job was green twice earlier while every transport test silently skipped.\n\nMETHOD-BY-METHOD, checked against the criterion this time rather than assumed:\n  create_issue, get_issue, update_issue, transition_issue_by_name, add_label, search_issues,\n  set_relationship, get_issuelinks_map, map_remote_links, link_payload_for_relation,\n  add_comment, get_comment_map, probe_remote — all 13 covered by an executing live test.\n\nLink CONTENT is asserted through the direct issue endpoint, never search (ADR 0037: the search index\nlags writes by an unbounded interval, so a fresh-link assertion via search would be flaky by\nconstruction); the search-backed get_issuelinks_map is held to its shape contract only.\nmap_remote_links is driven with the REAL server issuelinks payload rather than a fixture — a fixture\nwould only prove the canonicalizer handles the shape we imagined."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785457087635065001,"uuid":"32faa858-e477-4500-9043-5b135182f544"}